<%# Sample Logic Note shown from the "i" button next to the Logic Note field.
    "Use this format" builds the same note in the field from the details already
    filled in this Request for Proposal (subject, theme, items, vendor, date) and
    leaves [ ] placeholders only for what the maker has to explain.
    locals: approver ("Director" or "COO", from Procurement Settings) %>
<% approver = local_assigns[:approver].presence || "Director" %>
<div class="logic-note-help" id="logic-note-help" data-logic-note-help hidden>
  <div class="logic-note-help__head">
    <strong>Logic Note format (example)</strong>
    <div class="logic-note-help__actions">
      <button type="button" class="app-secondary-btn" data-logic-note-use>Use this format</button>
      <button type="button" class="logic-note-help__close" data-logic-note-close aria-label="Close format">&times;</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="logic-note-help__sample">
    <p class="logic-note-help__title">LOGIC NOTE<br><span>Procurement of Laptops for IT Department</span></p>
    <p class="logic-note-help__meta">Request for Proposal | Quotation Value: Above 10K | Single Vendor | Approval: <%= approver %></p>

    <h5>1. Requirement</h5>
    <p>The IT Department needs 2 laptops for the new field data officers who record vendor registrations, quotations and goods receipts in Apurti. The present systems are shared and cannot be spared for field visits.</p>

    <h5>2. Item-wise Requirement &amp; Estimated Cost</h5>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Qty</th><th>Max Rate (Rs.)</th><th>Amount (Rs.)</th><th>Remark</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td>Laptop (i5, 16 GB RAM)</td><td>2</td><td>50,000</td><td>1,00,000</td><td>One per field data officer</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>

    <h5>3. Reason for a Single Vendor</h5>
    <p>Shivam Office Systems is the only authorised dealer for this model registered with us in the district and gives on-site warranty service. Quotations from 3 vendors are not possible for this configuration within the required time.</p>

    <h5>4. Vendor Details</h5>
    <p>Shivam Office Systems is an approved vendor in Apurti for the IT Department theme and has supplied similar items to the organisation before.</p>

    <h5>5. Delivery &amp; Payment Terms</h5>
    <p>Delivery at the office within 15 days of the Purchase Order. Payment after goods receive and invoice verification.</p>

    <h5>6. Declaration</h5>
    <p>The amounts above are based on the internal max rate; the final value will be as per the vendor's quotation. The Purchase Order will be issued after the <%= approver %>'s approval.</p>
  </div>

  <template data-logic-note-template>LOGIC NOTE
Procurement of {{subject}}
Request for Proposal | Theme: {{theme}} | Quotation Value: Above 10K | Single Vendor | Approval: <%= approver %>

1. Requirement
[Why this material is needed, who will use it and where.]

2. Item-wise Requirement & Estimated Cost
{{items}}
Estimated total (as per max rate): Rs. {{total}}

3. Reason for a Single Vendor
[Why quotations from at least 3 vendors are not possible, e.g. only authorised dealer, proprietary item, only supplier in the area, urgency.]

4. Vendor Details
{{vendor}} - [why this vendor is suitable, e.g. approved vendor, past supply, service support.]

5. Delivery & Payment Terms
Delivery by {{end_date}} - [delivery location, installation, payment after goods receive and invoice verification.]

6. Declaration
The amounts above are based on the internal max rate; the final value will be as per the vendor's quotation. The Purchase Order will be issued after the <%= approver %>'s approval.</template>
</div>
